there's something real funky happening  in the mortgage market right now and  it's worth paying attention to if we go  back to 2020 when the pandemic struck  all of a sudden there was mass chaos in  financial markets stocks were down gold  was down bitcoin was down everything was  in a free fall of course we then had the  central banks and the politicians they  stepped in with massive monetary and  fiscal policies to try to correct the  situation the central bank went ahead  and had two emergency rate cuts they  brought interest rates down to zero  percent and their goal was to flood the  market with cheap capital if cheap  capital is available of course people  are going to go and they're going to  borrow well that's exactly what happened  and we saw mortgage applications both to  go and purchase homes but also to  refinance their existing debt absolutely  explode but now as the federal reserve  has started to raise interest rates we  get the mortgage rates at a 10 plus year  high mortgage rates haven't been this  high since 2010 and so what the hell is  going on in the market well if we take a  look here at the composite index what we  can see is this orange line that's the  mortgage rate on a 30-year fixed  mortgage and that blue line that shows  the mixture of both purchase and  refinance mortgage demand it exploded in  2020 but it's been coming down steadily  as that mortgage rate continued to rise  over the last few weeks then if we go  ahead and we take a look though and  let's break out the difference between  purchasing a home versus refinancing  your current debt the refinance index  shows that there has been a massive  drop-off all we're seeing is less and  less interest for people to refinance  now this makes sense because ultimately  refinancing is purely driven by the  monetary policy what do i mean if i'm a  homeowner already all i ask myself is  there cheaper capital out there than the  current capital that i have if the  answer is yes i refinance my mortgage if  the answer is no the capital that i  could go and get is not cheaper than i  don't refinance and so the main driver  of refinancing decisions is just what's  the rate for the mortgage if it's lower  i do it if it's not i don't but here's  the interesting thing and this is  something that we should pay attention  to here is that there's a difference  between what's happening in the  refinance demand market versus the  purchase demand market what am i talking  about well there's a complete decoupling  this black line shows refinancing and  the blue line shows the purchasing of a  home what you can see here on the far  right is in 2021 and into 2022 there's  been a complete decoupling less and less  people are refinancing but plenty of  people are still going and taking  mortgages because they're trying to  actually buy  a new home now when we ask ourselves why  that may be happening there's all kinds  of changes in work trends there's  obviously a rise of remote work  millennials are starting families and  moving into the suburbs and of course  there's tons of people who just want a  better work-life balance and don't want  to live in a shoebox in san francisco or  new york and that drives a lot of  purchasing decisions it's not just  monetary policy so ultimately that  decoupling is the intersection of the  monetary policy trend and the work trend  and the life trend and the work and life  trend is winning out right now now  refinances are down almost 60 percent  over the last 12 months and the demand  for purchasing a home is remaining  steady we got to be careful so for the  next five to ten years the united states  is going to have to become incredibly  proficient about building homes because  if we don't we're going to end up in a  situation with a worse imbalance between  supply and demand the average home in  america is now  starting at 500 000  that is absurd we're gonna have to fix  this problem or quite literally the  average american's not gonna be able to  afford a place to live hey you did you  like this video great we make five of  them a day and post them here on this  channel make sure you subscribe like the  video and see you next time
 

